\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, Saviour, Jesus, from above!
\par Assist me with Thy heavenly grace;
\par Empty my heart of earthly love,
\par And for Thyself prepare the place
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O let Thy sacred presence fill,
\par And set my longing spirit free!
\par Which pants to have no other will,
\par But day and night to feast on Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 3. That path with humble speed I'll seek,
\par Wherein my Saviour footsteps shine;
\par Nor will I hear, nor will I speak,
\par Of any other love but Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Henceforth may no profein delight
\par Divide this concecrated soul;
\par Possess it Thou, who hast the right,
\par As Lord and Master of the whole.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thee I can love, and Thee alone,
\par With pure delight and inward bliss:
\par To know Thou tak'st me for Thine own,
\par \pard\sl240\slmult1 O what a happiness in this!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Nothing on earth do I desire
\par But Thy pure love within my breast;
\par This, only this, will I require,
\par And freely give up all the rest.\f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

